This post is a simplified explanation of the paper “ReAct: Synergizing Reasoning and Acting in Language Models” by Yao et al., published on arXiv. All credit for the original research goes to the authors.

What you’ll read here is my personal understanding of the paper, along with simplified explanations of the core concepts — so you don’t have to spend hours deciphering the technicalities yourself.

Hope this helps, and I’m open to feedback — feel free to share your thoughts.

